{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    This function efficiently computes the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence iteratively.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n    else:\n        # Initialize with the first four values: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n        a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n        # Iteratively compute fib4(i) up to n\n        for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n            next_fib = a + b + c + d\n            a, b, c, d = b, c, d, next_fib\n        return d\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return sorted_l[n // 2]\n    else:\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "def modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p (be aware of numerics).\"\"\"\n    if p <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Modulus p must be a positive integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Exponent n must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 % p\n\n    result = 1\n    base = 2 % p\n    exponent = n\n\n    while exponent > 0:\n        if exponent % 2 == 1:\n            result = (result * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p\n        exponent //= 2\n    return result"}
