{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_prime_factor(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return the largest prime factor of n. Assume n > 1 and is not a prime.\"\"\"\n    largest_factor = 1\n\n    # Handle factor 2\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        largest_factor = 2\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Handle odd factors, checking up to sqrt(n)\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        while n % i == 0:\n            largest_factor = i\n            n //= i\n        i += 2 # Check only odd numbers\n\n    # If n is still greater than 2, it must be the largest prime factor\n    if n > 2:\n        largest_factor = n\n\n    return largest_factor\n```"}
