{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "```python\ndef derivative(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs represent coefficients of a polynomial.\n    xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[2] * x^2 + ....\n     Return derivative of this polynomial in the same form.\n    >>> derivative([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    [1, 4, 12, 20]\n    >>> derivative([1, 2, 3])\n    [2, 6]\n    \"\"\"\n    derivative_coeffs = []\n    # The derivative of c * x^i is i * c * x^(i-1).\n    # The constant term (index 0) becomes 0 and is dropped.\n    # Start iterating from the coefficient of x^1 (index 1).\n    for i in range(1, len(xs)):\n        derivative_coeffs.append(xs[i] * i)\n\n    return derivative_coeffs\n```"}
