{"task_id": "HumanEval/72", "solution": "def will_it_fly(q,w):\n    '''\n    Write a function that returns True if the object q will fly, and False otherwise.\n    The object q will fly if it's balanced (it is a palindromic list) and the sum of its elements is less than or equal the maximum possible weight w.\n    '''\n    is_balanced = (q == q[::-1])\n    total_weight = sum(q)\n    within_weight_limit = (total_weight <= w)\n\n    return is_balanced and within_weight_limit"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/77", "solution": "```python\ndef iscube(a):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer `a` is a perfect cube of some integer.\n    Handles positive, negative, and zero inputs, accounting for floating-point precision.\n    \"\"\"\n    if a == 0:\n        return True\n\n    # Calculate the absolute value for cube root computation\n    abs_a = abs(a)\n\n    # Calculate the cube root and round to the nearest integer to mitigate floating-point inaccuracies\n    cbrt_candidate = round(abs_a**(1/3))\n\n    # Check if the cube of the candidate equals the original absolute value\n    if a > 0:\n        return cbrt_candidate * cbrt_candidate * cbrt_candidate == a\n    else: # a < 0\n        # For negative numbers, the cube root will also be negative\n        return -cbrt_candidate * cbrt_candidate * cbrt_candidate == a\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/76", "solution": "```python\ndef is_simple_power(x, n):\n    \"\"\"Your task is to write a function that returns true if a number x is a simple\n    power of n and false in other cases.\n    x is a simple power of n if n**int=x\n    For example:\n    is_simple_power(1, 4) => true\n    is_simple_power(2, 2) => true\n    is_simple_power(8, 2) => true\n    is_simple_power(3, 2) => false\n    is_simple_power(3, 1) => false\n    is_simple_power(5, 3) => false\n    \"\"\"\n    if x == 1:\n        return True\n\n    if n == 1:\n        return False\n\n    while x > 1 and x % n == 0:\n        x //= n\n\n    return x == 1\n```"}
