{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "```python\ndef is_bored(S):\n    \"\"\"Counts sentences starting with \"I\" (case-insensitive), delimited by '.', '?', '!'.\n\n    For example:\n    >>> is_bored(\"Hello world\")\n    0\n    >>> is_bored(\"The sky is blue. The sun is shining. I love this weather\")\n    1\n    \"\"\"\n    SENTENCE_DELIMITERS = ['.', '?', '!']\n    boredom_count = 0\n\n    # Use a temporary marker to split sentences while preserving delimiters\n    temp_text = S\n    for delimiter in SENTENCE_DELIMITERS:\n        temp_text = temp_text.replace(delimiter, delimiter + \"[SPLIT_MARKER]\")\n\n    # Split by the marker, clean up whitespace, and filter out empty segments\n    sentences = [s.strip() for s in temp_text.split(\"[SPLIT_MARKER]\") if s.strip()]\n\n    for sentence in sentences:\n        cleaned_sentence = sentence.strip().lower()\n        if cleaned_sentence.startswith(\"i \") or cleaned_sentence == \"i\":\n            boredom_count += 1\n\n    return boredom_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/93", "solution": "```python\ndef encode(message):\n    \"\"\"\n    Encodes a message by swapping letter cases and replacing vowels with a letter two places ahead.\n    Non-letter characters are left unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    VOWELS = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n    ALPHABET = ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd', 'e', 'f', 'g', 'h', 'i', 'j', 'k', 'l', 'm', 'n', 'o', 'p', 'q', 'r', 's', 't', 'u', 'v', 'w', 'x', 'y', 'z']\n\n    encoded_chars = []\n    for char in message:\n        # First, swap case\n        if char.isalpha():\n            processed_char = char.swapcase()\n        else:\n            processed_char = char\n\n        # Then, replace vowels in the processed_char\n        lower_char = processed_char.lower()\n        if lower_char in VOWELS:\n            current_index = ALPHABET.index(lower_char)\n            new_index = (current_index + 2) % len(ALPHABET)\n            replaced_char = ALPHABET[new_index]\n\n            # Maintain original case of the replaced vowel\n            if processed_char.isupper():\n                processed_char = replaced_char.upper()\n            else:\n                processed_char = replaced_char\n\n        encoded_chars.append(processed_char)\n\n    return \"\".join(encoded_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/90", "solution": "def next_smallest(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    You are given a list of integers.\n    Write a function next_smallest() that returns the 2nd smallest element of the list.\n    Return None if there is no such element.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Convert the list to a set to get unique elements, then convert back to a list and sort.\n    unique_sorted_list = sorted(list(set(lst)))\n\n    # If there are fewer than two distinct elements, return None.\n    if len(unique_sorted_list) < 2:\n        return None\n    else:\n        # Otherwise, return the second element (index 1) which is the 2nd smallest.\n        return unique_sorted_list[1]"}
