{"task_id": "HumanEval/132", "solution": "```python\ndef is_nested(string):\n    '''\n    Checks if a string containing only square brackets has a valid nested subsequence.\n    A nested subsequence is defined as a pattern like '[[]]'.\n    '''\n    state = 0  # 0: looking for first '[', 1: looking for second '[',\n               # 2: looking for first ']', 3: looking for second ']'\n\n    for char in string:\n        if state == 0:\n            if char == '[':\n                state = 1\n        elif state == 1:\n            if char == '[':\n                state = 2\n            # If char is ']', we stay in state 1, as we need another '['\n        elif state == 2:\n            if char == ']':\n                state = 3\n            # If char is '[', we stay in state 2, as we need a ']'\n        elif state == 3:\n            if char == ']':\n                return True  # Found the nested subsequence '[[]]'\n            # If char is '[', we stay in state 3, as we need another ']'\n\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/130", "solution": "```python\ndef tri(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Tribonacci sequence up to the nth term.\n    Returns a list of the first n + 1 numbers of the Tribonacci sequence.\n    \"\"\"\n    _memo = {}\n\n    def _get_tribonacci_number(k):\n        if k in _memo:\n            return _memo[k]\n\n        result = None\n        if k == 0:\n            result = 1\n        elif k == 1:\n            result = 3\n        elif k % 2 == 0:  # Even number\n            result = 1 + k // 2\n        else:  # Odd number\n            val_k_minus_1 = _get_tribonacci_number(k - 1)\n            val_k_minus_2 = _get_tribonacci_number(k - 2)\n            val_k_plus_1 = _get_tribonacci_number(k + 1)\n            result = val_k_minus_1 + val_k_minus_2 + val_k_plus_1\n\n        _memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    sequence = []\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        sequence.append(_get_tribonacci_number(i))\n    return sequence\n```"}
